      "comment": "One radial spoke of the self-built STAR-TENT: a 1.5 m aluminium LED profile carrying 23 pixels, driven per pixel over Art-Net by a WLED node in per-pixel Multi RGB DMX mode (DMX_MODE_MULTIPLE_RGB, 3 ch/LED) -- not WLED effect mode, which is out of scope for Beamhouse v1. The physical device is ONE WLED node driving TEN of these spokes as a single 230-LED run over two buses (LEDs 0-137 on pin 5, 138-229 on pin 16). Ten spokes at ten angles are not collinear, so ADR-0005 makes each 23-pixel spoke its own strip and ADR-0009 makes each spoke its own fixture: patch the tent as ten of these. Address table, spoke order and the serpentine cabling are in docs/research/obf26-definition-migration.md section 3. MEASURED (issue #21, read off the live node's hw.led.ins on 2026-09-02): 23 px per spoke, 230 px total, and the 6/4 bus split that proves the count. The 1.5 m profile length is stated by the rig owner. DERIVED, NOT MEASURED: the 65.217 mm pitch is 1500/23, i.e. the pixels tiling the profile. If instead the first and last pixel sit at the profile's ends the pitch is 1500/22 = 68.182 mm, 4.6% larger. One tape measure settles it; nothing here depends on it yet. PLACEHOLDER: the 20 mm cross-section is nominal and unmeasured. No v1 render path reads it -- ADR-0005 takes ordering, axis and extent from pixel positions and nothing else. matrixPixels.spacing is the GAP between pixels in OFL, not the pitch, so the whole 65.217 mm cell is declared as the pixel's own dimension with a zero gap -- the idiom 13 of the 17 matrixPixels fixtures in the OFL .aglight export use. The emitters are physically RGB + CW + WW (FW1906, bus type 28), but WLED's per-pixel DMX modes top out at 4 ch/LED and derive CW/WW on-device, so there is no wire path to the white channels in any mode. RGB here is the protocol's limit, not a v1 concession. Authored for the Beamhouse project; not an upstream Open Fixture Library fixture. Replaces the superseded 'WLED T8 Pixel Tube 35px' (issue #6), whose pixel count, unit count and segment-to-fixture mapping were all falsified by #21.",
